          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Binary Search Fundamentals"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Binary Search finds a target in a ==sorted array== by halving the space. Cost: **at most log₂(n)** comparisons.",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Mid Calculation",
          "items": [
            "`mid = low + (high - low) / 2`",
            "low = start, high = end",
            "mid = middle index",
            "Why? `(low + high)` can **overflow**"
          ],
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Prerequisites",
          "items": [
            "Array / search space must be **sorted**",
            "==Random access== to elements"
          ],
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Time & Space Complexity",
          "items": [
            "Time: ==O(log n)==",
            "Space: O(1) iterative",
            "Space: O(log n) recursive"
          ],
          "ink": "blue"
        },
