          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Binary Search on Answer"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Search on the ==ANSWER==, not on the array",
            "Use when the answer can't be found directly",
            "But we CAN check if a given answer is **POSSIBLE**",
            "Every mid is a candidate answer to test"
          ],
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "java",
          "lines": [
            "long ans = -1; // or high",
            "while (low <= high) {",
            "  mid = low + (high - low) / 2;",
            "  if (isPossible(mid)) {",
            "    ans = mid;      // store",
            "    high = mid - 1; // try smaller",
            "  } else low = mid + 1; // larger",
            "}",
            "return ans;"
          ],
          "note": "isPossible(mid) must be monotonic"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "IMPORTANT",
          "text": "high = mid - 1 hunts the **MINIMUM** feasible answer. Use low = mid + 1 when you want the maximum."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Key idea: define a search space of possible answers, then test feasibility of mid. Feasible -> try a ==better== (smaller) answer; not feasible -> go larger. Works only when the condition is **MONOTONIC**.",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "5. Monotonic Condition",
          "items": [
            "As the answer grows, condition moves in ==one direction== only",
            "{green:F F F T T T} -> monotonic, possible",
            "{red:T F T F T F} -> not monotonic, not possible"
          ],
          "ink": "red"
        }
      ]
    },
